# BFSI Bank Customer Churn Analysis

An end-to-end Excel analytics project on a 10,000-customer retail bank portfolio: data quality checks, transformation, EDA, statistical summary, cross-tab analysis, an interactive dashboard, business Q&A, VBA macro source, and a full what-if / scenario analysis ending in a management recommendation.

## Headline findings

| Metric | Result |
|---|---|
| Overall churn rate | **20.37%** (2,037 of 10,000) |
| Balance held by churned customers | **$185.6M (24.26%** of portfolio balance) |
| Highest-risk geography | Germany, **32.44%** (France 16.15%, Spain 16.67%) |
| Highest-risk age band | 51-60, **56.21%** |
| Engagement gap | Inactive 26.85% vs Active 14.27% |
| Product count | 2 products safest (7.58%); 3-4 products 83-100% |
| Not drivers | CreditScore, Salary, Tenure (near-zero correlation) |

**Key insight:** churn *rate* and balance *protected* are different goals. Broad levers reach a 15% churn target easily, but protecting 80% of at-risk balance also requires a dedicated high-value retention track.

